          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em kernel
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            is that part of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
            which is sent to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero"} zero
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p There are various definitions of the notion of kernel, depending on the properties and structures available in the ambient category. We list a few definitions and discuss (in parts) when they are equivalent.
          %h3#as_a_pullback As a pullback
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              In a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              with an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
              %strong kernel
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(f)
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: A \to B
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(f) \to A
              along
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              of the unique morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \to B
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ker
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    ker(f)
                    \&amp;\to&amp;
                    0
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{p}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    A &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; B
                    }
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              More explicitly, this characterizes the object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(f)
              as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
              object (unique up to unique
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            %p
              for every object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and every morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h : C \to A
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi h
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\circ h = 0
              is the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+morphism"} zero morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : C \to ker(f)
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo =
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h = p\circ \phi
          %h3#as_an_equalizer As an equalizer
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              In a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+morphism"} zero morphisms
              (meaning:
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
              over the
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+pointed+sets"} category of pointed sets
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
              %strong kernel
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(f)
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi c
                    %mo →
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : c \to d
              is, if it exists, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalizer"} equalizer
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              and the zero morphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mn 0
                        %mrow
                          %mi c
                          %mo ,
                          %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0_{c,d}
          %h3#as_a_weighted_limit As a weighted limit
          %p
            In any category enriched over pointed sets, the kernel of a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi c
                  %mo →
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:c\to d
            is the universal morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo :
                  %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k:a\to c
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \circ k
            is the basepoint. It is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted limit
            in the sense of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive category
          %p
            This is a special case of the construction of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+kernels"} generalized kernels
            in enriched categories.
          %h3#AsARepresentingObject As a representing object
          %p
            Let
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
          %p
            In every
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X\to Y
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subfunctor"} subfunctor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ker
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker f \colon A^{op}\to Ab
          %p
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom(-,X)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ker
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi ker
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Z
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Z
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (ker f)(Z) = ker\big(hom(Z,X)\to hom(Z,Y)\big),
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ker
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker
            on the right-hand side is the kernel in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
          %p
            If the category is in fact
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preabelian+category"} preabelian
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ker
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker f
            is also representable with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representing+object"} representing object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ker
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ker f
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Coker
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Coker f
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi coker
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} coker f
            defined as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi coker
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi coker
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Z
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Z
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (coker f)(Z) = coker\big(hom(Z,X)\to hom(Z,Y)\big)
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            construction, one should
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/corepresentable+functor"} co-represent
            another functor, namely, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+functor"} covariant functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi ker
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z\mapsto ker\big(hom(Y,Z) \to hom(X,Z)\big)
            (which is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+object"} quotent
            of the corepresentable functor
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom(X,-)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Coker
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Coker f
            is defined by the “double dualization” (passing to
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+categories"} opposite categories
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Coker
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Ker
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mi op
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Coker f = (Ker f^{op})^{op}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            from its corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
          %h3#in_an_category
            In an
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            The kernel of a morphism in an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            with
            = succeed "-categorical" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+object"} zero object
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            as in the pullback definition above: the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
          %p
            See also
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} stable (∞,1)-category
          %h3#other_meanings Other meanings
          %p
            In some fields, the term ‘kernel’ refers to an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            that category theorists would see as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel+pair"} kernel pair
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            theory where both notions exist but are not equivalent (while in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            theory they are equivalent).
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            theory, even when one assumes that rings have units preserved by ring homomorphisms, the traditional notion of kernel (an
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+algebra"} universal algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Malcev+variety"} Mal'cev varieties
          %p Kashiwara-Schapira, following the terminology of EGA, uses kernel as a synonym of equalizer (and co-kernel of co-equalizer).
          %h2#Properties Properties
          .num_prop
            %h6#property Property
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be a category with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullbacks
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+object"} zero object
            %p
              In
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By the
              %a{:href => "http://nlab.mathforge.org/nlab/show/pullback#Pasting"} pasting law for pullbacks
              we have that the total square
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ker
                            %mi ker
                            %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi ker
                            %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi c
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    ker ker f &amp;\to&amp; ker f  &amp;\to&amp; 0
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    0 &amp;\to&amp; c &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; d
                    }
            %p
              is a pullback. Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \to c
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              and the pullback of a monomorphism along itself is the domain of the monomorphis, we have
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ker
                      %mi ker
                      %mi f
                      %mo ≃
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker ker f \simeq 0
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              This statement crucially fails to be true in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"} loop space object
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequence"} short exact sequences
              in 1-category theory, there are instead long
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+sequence"} fiber sequences
              in higher category theory.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              In a category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullbacks
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushouts
              and a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+object"} zero object
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
              form a pair of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functors
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} arrow categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi coker
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi Arr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mi ker
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi coker
                    %mi Arr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (coker \dashv ker) : Arr(C) \stackrel{\overset{coker}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{ker}{\to}} Arr(C)
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              We check the hom-isomorphism of a pair of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functors
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Arr
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ker
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Arr_C(g,ker f)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi c
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi ker
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi d
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi b
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    c &amp;\to&amp; ker(f) &amp;\to&amp; 0
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{g}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    d &amp;\to&amp; a &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; b
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the universal property of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi c
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi d
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi b
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    c  &amp;\to&amp; &amp;\to&amp; 0
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{g}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    d &amp;\to&amp; a &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; b
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the dual reasoning, an element in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Arr
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi coker
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Arr_C(coker g, f)
              is a diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi c
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mi d
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi coker
                            %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi b
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    c &amp;\stackrel{g}{\to}&amp; d &amp;\to&amp; a
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    0 &amp;\to&amp; coker g &amp;\to&amp; b
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the universal property of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
              this is equivalently a diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi c
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mi d
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi b
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    c &amp;\stackrel{g}{\to}&amp; d &amp;\to&amp; a
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp;  &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    0 &amp;\to&amp;  &amp;\to&amp; b
                    }
                    \\,.
          %p
            (This also follows from the general theory of
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+kernels"} generalized kernels
          %h2#examples Examples
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              In the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
              of abelian groups, the kernel of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+homomorphism"} group homomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : A \to B
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              on the set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(0)
              of elements of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              that are sent to the zero-element of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              More generally, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              any
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"} Mod
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preimage"} preimage
              of the zero-element at the level of the underlying sets, equipped with the unique sub-module structure on that set.
